## Device

Each part of the device contract (`device` in the API, the same traits as other WireWeaver devices) has its own
`{{ s.cli }}` command. Stop `just run` first; `just flash` and `just run` put the firmware's ELF into the ELF directory
(`cnt elf add`), so `counters`, `log` and `report` find it by the build id the board reports (`--elf FILE` names one,
`--force` takes it although its build id differs).

```sh
{{ (s.cli ~ ' firmware').ljust(24) }} # name, version, git commit, build time and profile, build id
{{ (s.cli ~ ' board').ljust(24) }} # {{ B.get("product", o.name) }}{{ " rev " ~ B.get("revision") if B.get("revision") else "" }} (Assumed), serial = the chip's unique id
{{ (s.cli ~ ' uid').ljust(24) }} # the {{ s.uid_bits }}-bit unique id
{% if s.dev_variant %}
{{ (s.cli ~ ' variant').ljust(24) }} # {{ R.get("variant", "the chip's id, revision and flash size") }}: DBGMCU_IDCODE and the flash size register
{% endif %}
{% if o.settings_flash %}
{{ (s.cli ~ ' label "bench 1"').ljust(24) }} # the label, in flash; `{{ s.cli }} label` shows it
{% endif %}
{% if o.crash %}
{{ (s.cli ~ ' last-reset').ljust(24) }} # reset cause and boot count, the crash record after a HardFault or panic
{% endif %}
{% if o.counters %}
{{ (s.cli ~ ' counters').ljust(24) }} # every cnt counter, RAM{{ " and backup registers" if o.bkp else "" }}
{{ s.cli }} counters --reset ram
{% endif %}
{% if s.dev_log %}
{{ (s.cli ~ ' log').ljust(24) }} # the defmt log the board keeps, decoded; the board keeps it as it is
{{ (s.cli ~ ' log -f').ljust(24) }} # then every new line as it is logged, until Ctrl-C
{% endif %}
{% if o.settings_flash %}
{{ (s.cli ~ ' settings show').ljust(24) }} # {{ "led-at-boot" if o.led else "the settings" }}
{% if o.led %}
{{ (s.cli ~ ' settings led-at-boot on').ljust(32) }} # {{ R.get("led", "the LED") }} lights at boot (try it: press RESET{{ ", " ~ R.get("reset") if R.get("reset") else "" }})
{% endif %}
{{ (s.cli ~ ' settings reset').ljust(24) }} # every setting back to its default, the label too
{% endif %}
{% if s.rom_boot %}
